<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Performance comparison for different methods across varying color bits on CIFAR-10, CIFAR-100, and Tiny-ImageNet datasets.
Mean and standard deviation are computed from 5 independent runs.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OCTree</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gervautz and Purgathofer, 1988</a>)</cite> builds an octree data structure where each node represents a color or a group of similar colors. Starting with all colors of an image in the octree, the process iteratively merges nodes (colors) that are closest together until a target number of colors is reached.</p>
</div>
